cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PAD4-DB v2, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "PAD4-DB v2: A Provenance-First Database of PAD4 Inhibitors with Activity Cliff Characterization and Source Independence Scoring"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-16"
doi: "[TBD — fill after Zenodo deposition]"
url: "https://github.com/[TBD]"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  PAD4-DB v2 is a curated, provenance-first database of 3,093 human PAD4
  (peptidylarginine deiminase 4) inhibitors integrated from 95 PubChem
  bioassays, ChEMBL, and BindingDB. The database provides consensus pIC50
  values, source independence scores distinguishing pipeline re-curation from
  genuine experimental replication, systematic activity cliff characterization
  (94 severe pairs, 90.4% MMP-validated), and cliff-hub annotations for four
  hub compounds in two structural classes covering 53.2% of severe cliff pairs.
  A 327,336-compound HTS structural reference is included. All curation scripts
  and audit trails are deposited for full reproducibility.
keywords:
  - PAD4
  - peptidylarginine deiminase
  - PAD4 inhibitors
  - activity cliffs
  - matched molecular pairs
  - structure-activity relationships
  - bioactivity database
  - drug discovery
  - machine learning benchmarking
  - source independence
